     Smørgrav <_d_e_s_@_F_r_e_e_B_S_D_._o_r_g>.  It uses the archive(3) library developed by
     Tim Kientzle <_k_i_e_n_t_z_l_e_@_F_r_e_e_B_S_D_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     The bbssdduunnzziipp utility performs two scans of the command-line for arguments
     before and after the archive name, so as to maintain compatibility with
     Info-ZIP unzip.  As a result, the POSIX ‘--’ double-dash string used to
     separate options from arguments will need to be repeated.  For example,
     to extract a "-a.jpg" from "-b.zip" with overwrite, one would need to in‐
     voke
           bsdunzip -o -- -a.jpg -- -b.zip

